  "methodology": "Production React in headless Chromium. Each library renders the same controlled tree, from the bench file in the module's __benches__ folder; a value is the median ms across rounds, with the libraries interleaved and their order alternated per round, and a garbage collection forced before each timed phase. \"x100\" is a hundred copies rendered at once; overlays mount and unmount closed, and \"unmount open\" tears down a hundred once every one shows. Each value is the main thread's work, read from a Chromium trace, from the step until two frames after its result shows, less the harness's own work for each of those frames, measured over frames with nothing to do: an effect that mounts the content, a later task that positions it, a frame-late unmount, and the style, layout and paint of the frame showing it all count, and idle time between them does not. After mounting and after an update the page settles, until two frames pass with nothing changed, so the next step does not pay for work the last one left behind. \"open\" and \"close\" are one overlay. \"type\" sets every copy's input and dispatches its input event, as typing does, and runs until every copy shows the change. A duckVs ratio under 1 means gentleduck is faster than that library.",
